                    "patching_rect": [ 26.0, 89.0, 1372.0, 21.0 ],
                    "presentation": 1,
                    "presentation_rect": [ 26.0, 45.0, 1372.0, 21.0 ],
                    "text": "Choose a description below. Copy the SFZ example into an instrument file. Examples include companion settings; filenames marked REPLACE_WITH must be supplied.",
                    "textcolor": [ 0.12, 0.18, 0.24, 1.0 ]
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "coll_data": {
                        "count": 507,
                        "data": [
                            {
                                "key": 1,
                                "value": [ "#define $WAVE *sine", "Instrument Settings / #define   ·   entry 001", "VALUES: #define $NAME replacement-text\nSCOPE: preprocessor (outside headers)", "Defines a preprocessor substitution; this directive does not use an equals sign.", "A $NAME macro must be referenced later in the file; defining it alone changes no sound.", "// #define — Instrument Settings\n#define $WAVE *sine\n<region>\nsample=$WAVE lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Instrument Settings / #define   ·   entry 001\nVALUES: #define $NAME replacement-text\nSCOPE: preprocessor (outside headers)\nREQUIRES: A $NAME macro must be referenced later in the file; defining it alone changes no sound.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 2,
                                "value": [ "default_path=samples/", "Instrument Settings / default_path   ·   entry 002", "VALUES: directory path string\nSCOPE: <control>", "In <control>, sets the base directory for sample-file references.", "The samples/ folder must exist relative to the SFZ file; put the named sample inside it. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.", "// default_path — Instrument Settings\n<control>\ndefault_path=samples/\n<region>\nsample=REPLACE_WITH_SAMPLE.wav lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-18 ampeg_release=0.25\n", "Replace the filename, keep <control> before the region, then play note 60.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Instrument Settings / default_path   ·   entry 002\nVALUES: directory path string\nSCOPE: <control>\nREQUIRES: The samples/ folder must exist relative to the SFZ file; put the named sample inside it. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.\nTRY: Replace the filename, keep <control> before the region, then play note 60.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 3,
                                "value": [ "note_offset=12", "Instrument Settings / note_offset   ·   entry 003", "VALUES: int · -127…127 semitones [P]\nSCOPE: <control>", "In <control>, shifts mapped note numbers by this many semitones.", "No companion opcode required; use a mapped region and note events. Offsets change key mapping, so compare both note 60 and its shifted note.", "// note_offset — Instrument Settings\n<control>\nnote_offset=12\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25\n", "Play notes across the mapped keyboard range; the example note offset changes which keys trigger the region.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Instrument Settings / note_offset   ·   entry 003\nVALUES: int · -127…127 semitones [P]\nSCOPE: <control>\nREQUIRES: No companion opcode required; use a mapped region and note events. Offsets change key mapping, so compare both note 60 and its shifted note.\nTRY: Play notes across the mapped keyboard range; the example note offset changes which keys trigger the region.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 4,
                                "value": [ "octave_offset=1", "Instrument Settings / octave_offset   ·   entry 004", "VALUES: int · -10…10 octaves [P]\nSCOPE: <control>", "In <control>, shifts mapped note numbers by this many octaves.", "No companion opcode required; use a mapped region and note events. Offsets change key mapping, so compare both note 60 and its shifted note.", "// octave_offset — Instrument Settings\n<control>\noctave_offset=1\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25\n", "Play notes across the mapped keyboard range; the example note offset changes which keys trigger the region.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Instrument Settings / octave_offset   ·   entry 004\nVALUES: int · -10…10 octaves [P]\nSCOPE: <control>\nREQUIRES: No companion opcode required; use a mapped region and note events. Offsets change key mapping, so compare both note 60 and its shifted note.\nTRY: Play notes across the mapped keyboard range; the example note offset changes which keys trigger the region.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 5,
                                "value": [ "label_cc1=Modulation wheel", "Instrument Settings / label_ccN   ·   entry 005", "VALUES: text; N=0…127 for ordinary MIDI CCs\nSCOPE: <control>", "In <control>, assigns metadata text to a controller; Max has no automatic label display.", "Metadata only: no audible dependency and no automatic label display in Max sfizz~.", "// label_ccN — Instrument Settings\n<control>\nlabel_cc1=Modulation wheel\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Metadata; loading it will not create a Max control or change sound.", "Instrument Settings / label_ccN   ·   entry 005\nVALUES: text; N=0…127 for ordinary MIDI CCs\nSCOPE: <control>\nREQUIRES: Metadata only: no audible dependency and no automatic label display in Max sfizz~.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Metadata; loading it will not create a Max control or change sound." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 6,
                                "value": [ "label_key60=Middle C", "Instrument Settings / label_keyN   ·   entry 006", "VALUES: text; N=0…127\nSCOPE: <control>", "In <control>, assigns metadata text to a MIDI key; this does not alter its pitch.", "Metadata only: no audible dependency and no automatic label display in Max sfizz~.", "// label_keyN — Instrument Settings\n<control>\nlabel_key60=Middle C\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Metadata; loading it will not create a Max control or change sound.", "Instrument Settings / label_keyN   ·   entry 006\nVALUES: text; N=0…127\nSCOPE: <control>\nREQUIRES: Metadata only: no audible dependency and no automatic label display in Max sfizz~.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Metadata; loading it will not create a Max control or change sound." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 7,
                                "value": [ "set_cc1=64", "Instrument Settings / set_ccN   ·   entry 007", "VALUES: float · 0…127 [P]\nSCOPE: <control>", "In <control>, supplies a controller initial value; retained MIDI state can affect reload behavior.", "Requires a region mapping that uses the same CC, such as volume_oncc1; initialization alone does not assign a musical destination.", "// set_ccN — Instrument Settings\n<control>\nset_cc1=64\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-36\nampeg_release=0.25 volume_oncc1=30\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Instrument Settings / set_ccN   ·   entry 007\nVALUES: float · 0…127 [P]\nSCOPE: <control>\nREQUIRES: Requires a region mapping that uses the same CC, such as volume_oncc1; initialization alone does not assign a musical destination.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 8,
                                "value": [ "#include \"helpers/voice.sfz\"", "Instrument Settings / #include   ·   entry 008", "VALUES: #include \"relative/path.sfz\"\nSCOPE: preprocessor (outside headers)", "Inserts another SFZ text file at this position; this directive does not use an equals sign.", "The quoted include file must exist relative to the SFZ file and contain valid SFZ text.", "// #include — Instrument Settings\n// First create helpers/voice.sfz beside this file.\n// Contents of helpers/voice.sfz:\n// <region> sample=*sine key=60 volume=-18\n#include \"helpers/voice.sfz\"\n", "Create the helper file with the content shown, then load the parent SFZ and play note 60.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Instrument Settings / #include   ·   entry 008\nVALUES: #include \"relative/path.sfz\"\nSCOPE: preprocessor (outside headers)\nREQUIRES: The quoted include file must exist relative to the SFZ file and contain valid SFZ text.\nTRY: Create the helper file with the content shown, then load the parent SFZ and play note 60.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 9,
                                "value": [ "set_hdcc1=0.5", "Instrument Settings / set_hdccN   ·   entry 009", "VALUES: float · 0…1 [P]\nSCOPE: <control>", "In <control>, supplies a normalized high-resolution controller initial value.", "Requires a region mapping that uses the same CC, such as volume_oncc1; initialization alone does not assign a musical destination.", "// set_hdccN — Instrument Settings\n<control>\nset_hdcc1=0.5\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-36\nampeg_release=0.25 volume_oncc1=30\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Instrument Settings / set_hdccN   ·   entry 009\nVALUES: float · 0…1 [P]\nSCOPE: <control>\nREQUIRES: Requires a region mapping that uses the same CC, such as volume_oncc1; initialization alone does not assign a musical destination.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 10,
                                "value": [ "set_realcc1=0.5", "Instrument Settings / set_realccN   ·   entry 010", "VALUES: float · 0…1 [P]\nSCOPE: <control>", "In <control>, supplies a normalized high-resolution controller initial value.", "Requires a region mapping that uses the same CC, such as volume_oncc1; initialization alone does not assign a musical destination.", "// set_realccN — Instrument Settings\n<control>\nset_realcc1=0.5\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-36\nampeg_release=0.25 volume_oncc1=30\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Instrument Settings / set_realccN   ·   entry 010\nVALUES: float · 0…1 [P]\nSCOPE: <control>\nREQUIRES: Requires a region mapping that uses the same CC, such as volume_oncc1; initialization alone does not assign a musical destination.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 11,
                                "value": [ "hint_stealing=oldest", "Instrument Settings / hint_stealing   ·   entry 011", "VALUES: first | oldest | envelope_and_age\nSCOPE: <control>", "In <control>, selects how the engine chooses a voice to steal at the voice limit.", "Only observable when overlapping notes exceed a voice/polyphony limit.", "// hint_stealing — Instrument Settings\n<control>\nhint_stealing=oldest\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 polyphony=2\n", "Hold three or more notes in 48…72 with polyphony=2 and compare which older voice is removed.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Instrument Settings / hint_stealing   ·   entry 011\nVALUES: first | oldest | envelope_and_age\nSCOPE: <control>\nREQUIRES: Only observable when overlapping notes exceed a voice/polyphony limit.\nTRY: Hold three or more notes in 48…72 with polyphony=2 and compare which older voice is removed.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 12,
                                "value": [ "hint_ram_based=1", "Instrument Settings / hint_ram_based   ·   entry 012", "VALUES: on | off (also 1 | 0)\nSCOPE: <control>", "In <control>, requests whole samples in RAM instead of normal disk streaming.", "Use a real sample file; the change concerns sample loading, not a musical parameter. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.", "// hint_ram_based — Instrument Settings\n<control>\nhint_ram_based=1\n<region>\nsample=REPLACE_WITH_SAMPLE.wav lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-18 ampeg_release=0.25\n", "Replace the sample path and compare loading/streaming behavior rather than expecting a timbre change.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Instrument Settings / hint_ram_based   ·   entry 012\nVALUES: on | off (also 1 | 0)\nSCOPE: <control>\nREQUIRES: Use a real sample file; the change concerns sample loading, not a musical parameter. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.\nTRY: Replace the sample path and compare loading/streaming behavior rather than expecting a timbre change.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 13,
                                "value": [ "hint_sustain_cancels_release=1", "Instrument Settings / hint_sustain_cancels_release   ·   entry 013", "VALUES: on | off (also 1 | 0)\nSCOPE: <control>", "In <control>, allows a newly pressed sustain pedal to cancel a voice release.", "Needs a voice still in its release stage and a sustain-pedal-down event during that release.", "// hint_sustain_cancels_release — Instrument Settings\n<control>\nhint_sustain_cancels_release=1\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18 ampeg_release=3\nsustain_cc=64 sustain_sw=on\n", "Play/release note 60, then send midievent 176 64 127 before its 3-second release ends; release the pedal with value 0.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Instrument Settings / hint_sustain_cancels_release   ·   entry 013\nVALUES: on | off (also 1 | 0)\nSCOPE: <control>\nREQUIRES: Needs a voice still in its release stage and a sustain-pedal-down event during that release.\nTRY: Play/release note 60, then send midievent 176 64 127 before its 3-second release ends; release the pedal with value 0.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 14,
                                "value": [ "count=3", "Sample Playback / count   ·   entry 014", "VALUES: int · 0…4294967295\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Sets the total sample plays and forces one_shot; in this engine 0 and 1 both play once.", "A finite sample is needed; count forces one_shot, so note-off does not end the repeated playback. Envelope stages are not retriggered for each repeat. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.", "// count — Sample Playback\n<region>\nsample=REPLACE_WITH_SAMPLE.wav lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-18 ampeg_release=0.25 count=3\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Sample Playback / count   ·   entry 014\nVALUES: int · 0…4294967295\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: A finite sample is needed; count forces one_shot, so note-off does not end the repeated playback. Envelope stages are not retriggered for each repeat. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 15,
                                "value": [ "delay=0.25", "Sample Playback / delay   ·   entry 015", "VALUES: float · 0…100 s [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Waits this long after a trigger before starting the sample.", "A note must remain active until the delayed start (unless one_shot behavior is used); releasing too early can suppress the sample. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.", "// delay — Sample Playback\n<region>\nsample=REPLACE_WITH_SAMPLE.wav lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-18 ampeg_release=0.25 delay=0.25\n", "Use a real sample; hold note 60 longer than the chosen delay.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Sample Playback / delay   ·   entry 015\nVALUES: float · 0…100 s [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: A note must remain active until the delayed start (unless one_shot behavior is used); releasing too early can suppress the sample. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.\nTRY: Use a real sample; hold note 60 longer than the chosen delay.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 16,
                                "value": [ "delay_cc1=0.5", "Sample Playback / delay_ccN   ·   entry 016", "VALUES: float · 0…100 s [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Adds a CC-scaled delay before the sample starts.", "A note must remain active until the delayed start (unless one_shot behavior is used); releasing too early can suppress the sample. Use MIDI CC 1, matching the numbered suffix; the example supplies its initial value in <control>. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.", "// delay_ccN — Sample Playback\n<control>\nset_cc1=64\n<region>\nsample=REPLACE_WITH_SAMPLE.wav lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-18 ampeg_release=0.25 delay_cc1=0.5\n", "Use a real sample; hold note 60 longer than the chosen delay. For note-start parameters, set MIDI CC 1 before each new note; compare values 0 and 127.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Sample Playback / delay_ccN   ·   entry 016\nVALUES: float · 0…100 s [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: A note must remain active until the delayed start (unless one_shot behavior is used); releasing too early can suppress the sample. Use MIDI CC 1, matching the numbered suffix; the example supplies its initial value in <control>. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.\nTRY: Use a real sample; hold note 60 longer than the chosen delay. For note-start parameters, set MIDI CC 1 before each new note; compare values 0 and 127.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 17,
                                "value": [ "delay_oncc1=0.5", "Sample Playback / delay_onccN   ·   entry 017", "VALUES: float · 0…100 s [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Adds a CC-scaled delay before the sample starts.", "A note must remain active until the delayed start (unless one_shot behavior is used); releasing too early can suppress the sample. Use MIDI CC 1, matching the numbered suffix; the example supplies its initial value in <control>. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.", "// delay_onccN — Sample Playback\n<control>\nset_cc1=64\n<region>\nsample=REPLACE_WITH_SAMPLE.wav lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-18 ampeg_release=0.25 delay_oncc1=0.5\n", "Use a real sample; hold note 60 longer than the chosen delay. For note-start parameters, set MIDI CC 1 before each new note; compare values 0 and 127.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Sample Playback / delay_onccN   ·   entry 017\nVALUES: float · 0…100 s [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: A note must remain active until the delayed start (unless one_shot behavior is used); releasing too early can suppress the sample. Use MIDI CC 1, matching the numbered suffix; the example supplies its initial value in <control>. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.\nTRY: Use a real sample; hold note 60 longer than the chosen delay. For note-start parameters, set MIDI CC 1 before each new note; compare values 0 and 127.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 18,
                                "value": [ "delay_random=0.4", "Sample Playback / delay_random   ·   entry 018", "VALUES: float · 0…100 s [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Adds a random start delay from zero up to this amount.", "A note must remain active until the delayed start (unless one_shot behavior is used); releasing too early can suppress the sample. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.", "// delay_random — Sample Playback\n<region>\nsample=REPLACE_WITH_SAMPLE.wav lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-18 ampeg_release=0.25 delay_random=0.4\n", "Use a real sample; hold note 60 longer than the chosen delay.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Sample Playback / delay_random   ·   entry 018\nVALUES: float · 0…100 s [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: A note must remain active until the delayed start (unless one_shot behavior is used); releasing too early can suppress the sample. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.\nTRY: Use a real sample; hold note 60 longer than the chosen delay.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
