                                "key": 48,
                                "value": [ "output=1", "Voice Lifecycle / output   ·   entry 048", "VALUES: int · 0…floor(outputs/2)−1; Max maximum 511\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Routes the region to stereo pair 0=outlets 1/2, 1=3/4, etc.; set Max @outputs accordingly.", "Requires enough sfizz~ @outputs channels and connected destinations; output=1 needs outlets 3/4 (at least @outputs 4).", "// output — Voice Lifecycle\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 output=1\n", "Create sfizz~ @outputs 4, connect outlets 3/4 to your playback path, load this SFZ and play note 60.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Voice Lifecycle / output   ·   entry 048\nVALUES: int · 0…floor(outputs/2)−1; Max maximum 511\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Requires enough sfizz~ @outputs channels and connected destinations; output=1 needs outlets 3/4 (at least @outputs 4).\nTRY: Create sfizz~ @outputs 4, connect outlets 3/4 to your playback path, load this SFZ and play note 60.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 49,
                                "value": [ "polyphony=2", "Voice Lifecycle / polyphony   ·   entry 049", "VALUES: int · 0…engine voice ceiling [B]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Limits simultaneous voices in its scope; the engine ceiling and Max @voices also apply.", "A voice limit is observed only with overlapping voices. note_selfmask requires note_polyphony and repeated notes of the same pitch.", "// polyphony — Voice Lifecycle\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18 ampeg_release=2\nnote_polyphony=1 polyphony=2\n", "Play overlapping notes; for note_polyphony/note_selfmask, repeatedly play note 60 at different velocities before older voices finish.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Voice Lifecycle / polyphony   ·   entry 049\nVALUES: int · 0…engine voice ceiling [B]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: A voice limit is observed only with overlapping voices. note_selfmask requires note_polyphony and repeated notes of the same pitch.\nTRY: Play overlapping notes; for note_polyphony/note_selfmask, repeatedly play note 60 at different velocities before older voices finish.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 50,
                                "value": [ "note_polyphony=1", "Voice Lifecycle / note_polyphony   ·   entry 050", "VALUES: int · 1…engine voice ceiling [B]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Limits simultaneous voices at the same pitch; the engine ceiling and Max @voices also apply.", "A voice limit is observed only with overlapping voices. note_selfmask requires note_polyphony and repeated notes of the same pitch.", "// note_polyphony — Voice Lifecycle\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18 ampeg_release=2\npolyphony=2 note_polyphony=1\n", "Play overlapping notes; for note_polyphony/note_selfmask, repeatedly play note 60 at different velocities before older voices finish.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Voice Lifecycle / note_polyphony   ·   entry 050\nVALUES: int · 1…engine voice ceiling [B]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: A voice limit is observed only with overlapping voices. note_selfmask requires note_polyphony and repeated notes of the same pitch.\nTRY: Play overlapping notes; for note_polyphony/note_selfmask, repeatedly play note 60 at different velocities before older voices finish.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 51,
                                "value": [ "note_selfmask=on", "Voice Lifecycle / note_selfmask   ·   entry 051", "VALUES: on | mask | off\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Chooses whether a softer repeated note can steal a louder voice under note_polyphony.", "A voice limit is observed only with overlapping voices. note_selfmask requires note_polyphony and repeated notes of the same pitch.", "// note_selfmask — Voice Lifecycle\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18 ampeg_release=2\npolyphony=2 note_polyphony=1 note_selfmask=on\n", "Play overlapping notes; for note_polyphony/note_selfmask, repeatedly play note 60 at different velocities before older voices finish.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Voice Lifecycle / note_selfmask   ·   entry 051\nVALUES: on | mask | off\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: A voice limit is observed only with overlapping voices. note_selfmask requires note_polyphony and repeated notes of the same pitch.\nTRY: Play overlapping notes; for note_polyphony/note_selfmask, repeatedly play note 60 at different velocities before older voices finish.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 52,
                                "value": [ "rt_dead=on", "Voice Lifecycle / rt_dead   ·   entry 052", "VALUES: on | off (also 1 | 0)\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Allows a release-trigger region even after the corresponding attack voice has ended.", "Only affects release-trigger regions; pair with an attack region on the same key and release after that short attack sample has ended. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.", "// rt_dead — Voice Lifecycle\n<region>\nsample=REPLACE_WITH_SHORT_ATTACK.wav lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-18 ampeg_release=0.25 key=60 loop_mode=one_shot\n<region>\nsample=REPLACE_WITH_RELEASE.wav lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-18 ampeg_release=0.25 key=60 trigger=release rt_dead=on\n", "Replace both sample paths; hold note 60 past the attack sample end, then release it.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Voice Lifecycle / rt_dead   ·   entry 052\nVALUES: on | off (also 1 | 0)\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Only affects release-trigger regions; pair with an attack region on the same key and release after that short attack sample has ended. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.\nTRY: Replace both sample paths; hold note 60 past the attack sample end, then release it.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
