                                "value": [ "volume_smoothcc1=80", "Amplifier / volume_smoothccN   ·   entry 109", "VALUES: int · 0…100 ms [P↑]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Smooths CC N changes to gain in dB over this time.", "A playable region and note event are sufficient; related parameters use their engine defaults unless the example sets them explicitly. Requires a nonzero volume_oncc1 amount using the same CC; smoothing/stepping/curve selection alone does not assign a modulation destination.", "// volume_smoothccN — Amplifier\n<control>\nset_cc1=64\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 volume_oncc1=30 volume_smoothcc1=80\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Amplifier / volume_smoothccN   ·   entry 109\nVALUES: int · 0…100 ms [P↑]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: A playable region and note event are sufficient; related parameters use their engine defaults unless the example sets them explicitly. Requires a nonzero volume_oncc1 amount using the same CC; smoothing/stepping/curve selection alone does not assign a modulation destination.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 110,
                                "value": [ "volume_stepcc1=1", "Amplifier / volume_stepccN   ·   entry 110", "VALUES: float · 0…127 dB [P↑]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Quantizes CC N modulation of gain in dB; 0 means continuous changes.", "A playable region and note event are sufficient; related parameters use their engine defaults unless the example sets them explicitly. Requires a nonzero volume_oncc1 amount using the same CC; smoothing/stepping/curve selection alone does not assign a modulation destination.", "// volume_stepccN — Amplifier\n<control>\nset_cc1=64\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 volume_oncc1=30 volume_stepcc1=1\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Amplifier / volume_stepccN   ·   entry 110\nVALUES: float · 0…127 dB [P↑]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: A playable region and note event are sufficient; related parameters use their engine defaults unless the example sets them explicitly. Requires a nonzero volume_oncc1 amount using the same CC; smoothing/stepping/curve selection alone does not assign a modulation destination.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 111,
                                "value": [ "width=0", "Amplifier / width   ·   entry 111", "VALUES: float · -100…100 % [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Sets stereo width; 0 collapses to mono, 100 is normal and −100 swaps channels.", "Pan needs an audible stereo output path; width/position require a stereo image to reshape (use a stereo sample). Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.", "// width — Amplifier\n<region>\nsample=REPLACE_WITH_STEREO.wav lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-18 ampeg_release=0.25 width=0\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Amplifier / width   ·   entry 111\nVALUES: float · -100…100 % [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Pan needs an audible stereo output path; width/position require a stereo image to reshape (use a stereo sample). Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 112,
                                "value": [ "width_oncc1=100", "Amplifier / width_onccN   ·   entry 112", "VALUES: float · -200…200 % [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Sets the CC N modulation amount for stereo width.", "Pan needs an audible stereo output path; width/position require a stereo image to reshape (use a stereo sample). Use MIDI CC 1, matching the numbered suffix; the example supplies its initial value in <control>. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.", "// width_onccN — Amplifier\n<control>\nset_cc1=64\n<region>\nsample=REPLACE_WITH_STEREO.wav lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-18 ampeg_release=0.25 width_oncc1=100\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Amplifier / width_onccN   ·   entry 112\nVALUES: float · -200…200 % [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Pan needs an audible stereo output path; width/position require a stereo image to reshape (use a stereo sample). Use MIDI CC 1, matching the numbered suffix; the example supplies its initial value in <control>. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
