                            {
                                "key": 116,
                                "value": [ "amp_keycenter=60", "Amplifier / amp_keycenter   ·   entry 116", "VALUES: note · 0…127 or C−1…G9\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Sets the reference key for amplitude key tracking.", "amp_keycenter matters only with nonzero amp_keytrack; play different keys to hear level tracking.", "// amp_keycenter — Amplifier\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 amp_keytrack=-1 amp_keycenter=60\n", "Compare notes 48, 60 and 72 at equal velocity.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Amplifier / amp_keycenter   ·   entry 116\nVALUES: note · 0…127 or C−1…G9\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: amp_keycenter matters only with nonzero amp_keytrack; play different keys to hear level tracking.\nTRY: Compare notes 48, 60 and 72 at equal velocity.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 117,
                                "value": [ "amp_keytrack=-1", "Amplifier / amp_keytrack   ·   entry 117", "VALUES: float · -96…12 dB [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Changes amplitude by this many dB per semitone from amp_keycenter.", "amp_keycenter matters only with nonzero amp_keytrack; play different keys to hear level tracking.", "// amp_keytrack — Amplifier\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 amp_keycenter=60 amp_keytrack=-1\n", "Compare notes 48, 60 and 72 at equal velocity.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Amplifier / amp_keytrack   ·   entry 117\nVALUES: float · -96…12 dB [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: amp_keycenter matters only with nonzero amp_keytrack; play different keys to hear level tracking.\nTRY: Compare notes 48, 60 and 72 at equal velocity.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 118,
                                "value": [ "amp_veltrack=100", "Amplifier / amp_veltrack   ·   entry 118", "VALUES: float · -100…100 % [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Sets velocity-to-amplitude tracking; 0 removes the usual velocity-dependent level.", "A playable region and note event are sufficient; related parameters use their engine defaults unless the example sets them explicitly.", "// amp_veltrack — Amplifier\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 amp_veltrack=100\n", "Compare notes at several velocities; 0 would remove ordinary velocity-dependent level.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Amplifier / amp_veltrack   ·   entry 118\nVALUES: float · -100…100 % [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: A playable region and note event are sufficient; related parameters use their engine defaults unless the example sets them explicitly.\nTRY: Compare notes at several velocities; 0 would remove ordinary velocity-dependent level.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 119,
                                "value": [ "amp_velcurve_64=0.25", "Amplifier / amp_velcurve_N   ·   entry 119", "VALUES: float · 0…1 [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Sets amplitude at velocity point N (N=0…127), with interpolation between defined points.", "Needs velocity tracking and multiple velocity values; defined curve points are interpolated between endpoints.", "// amp_velcurve_N — Amplifier\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 amp_velcurve_0=0 amp_velcurve_127=1 amp_veltrack=100\namp_velcurve_64=0.25\n", "Compare notes at velocities 32, 64 and 120.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Amplifier / amp_velcurve_N   ·   entry 119\nVALUES: float · 0…1 [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Needs velocity tracking and multiple velocity values; defined curve points are interpolated between endpoints.\nTRY: Compare notes at velocities 32, 64 and 120.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 120,
                                "value": [ "amp_random=6", "Amplifier / amp_random   ·   entry 120", "VALUES: float · -24…24 dB [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Sets the amount of per-voice random gain variation in dB.", "A playable region and note event are sufficient; related parameters use their engine defaults unless the example sets them explicitly.", "// amp_random — Amplifier\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 amp_random=6\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Amplifier / amp_random   ·   entry 120\nVALUES: float · -24…24 dB [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: A playable region and note event are sufficient; related parameters use their engine defaults unless the example sets them explicitly.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 121,
                                "value": [ "rt_decay=12", "Amplifier / rt_decay   ·   entry 121", "VALUES: float · 0…200 dB/s [P↑]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Attenuates release-trigger samples according to elapsed time since the attack note.", "Only meaningful on a release-trigger region paired with an attack note; attenuation depends on the time between note-on and release. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.", "// rt_decay — Amplifier\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 key=60\n<region>\nsample=REPLACE_WITH_RELEASE.wav lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-18 ampeg_release=0.25 key=60 trigger=release rt_dead=on rt_decay=12\n", "Replace the release-sample path; compare releasing note 60 after 0.2 seconds and after 3 seconds.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Amplifier / rt_decay   ·   entry 121\nVALUES: float · 0…200 dB/s [P↑]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Only meaningful on a release-trigger region paired with an attack note; attenuation depends on the time between note-on and release. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.\nTRY: Replace the release-sample path; compare releasing note 60 after 0.2 seconds and after 3 seconds.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 122,
                                "value": [ "xf_cccurve=power", "Amplifier / xf_cccurve   ·   entry 122", "VALUES: gain | power\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Selects a linear-gain or equal-power curve for controller, key or velocity crossfades.", "A crossfade needs ordered low/high endpoints; a curve-selector opcode only changes an existing fade. Add complementary regions for a crossfade between two sounds; one region simply fades.", "// xf_cccurve — Amplifier\n<control>\nset_cc1=64\n<region>\nsample=*saw lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 xfin_locc1=0 xfin_hicc1=127 xf_cccurve=power\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Amplifier / xf_cccurve   ·   entry 122\nVALUES: gain | power\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: A crossfade needs ordered low/high endpoints; a curve-selector opcode only changes an existing fade. Add complementary regions for a crossfade between two sounds; one region simply fades.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 123,
                                "value": [ "xf_keycurve=power", "Amplifier / xf_keycurve   ·   entry 123", "VALUES: gain | power\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Selects a linear-gain or equal-power curve for controller, key or velocity crossfades.", "A crossfade needs ordered low/high endpoints; a curve-selector opcode only changes an existing fade. Add complementary regions for a crossfade between two sounds; one region simply fades.", "// xf_keycurve — Amplifier\n<region>\nsample=*saw lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 xfin_lokey=48 xfin_hikey=60 xfout_lokey=60 xfout_hikey=72\nxf_keycurve=power\n", "Play chromatic notes from 48 through 72; endpoints can be silent.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Amplifier / xf_keycurve   ·   entry 123\nVALUES: gain | power\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: A crossfade needs ordered low/high endpoints; a curve-selector opcode only changes an existing fade. Add complementary regions for a crossfade between two sounds; one region simply fades.\nTRY: Play chromatic notes from 48 through 72; endpoints can be silent.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
