                            {
                                "key": 217,
                                "value": [ "ampeg_attackcc1=0.7", "Amplitude envelope / ampeg_attackccN   ·   entry 217", "VALUES: float · -100…100 s [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Sets CC N modulation of amplitude envelope attack time.", "The amplitude envelope has defaults, so each stage can work independently; hold the note long enough to reach the selected stage and send note-off to hear release. The same CC number must be sent; set it before triggering a new note for reliable envelope-stage comparisons.", "// ampeg_attackccN — Amplitude envelope\n<control>\nset_cc1=64\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.7 ampeg_attack=0.4 ampeg_decay=0.5 ampeg_sustain=40\nampeg_attackcc1=0.7\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. For note-start parameters, set MIDI CC 1 before each new note; compare values 0 and 127.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Amplitude envelope / ampeg_attackccN   ·   entry 217\nVALUES: float · -100…100 s [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: The amplitude envelope has defaults, so each stage can work independently; hold the note long enough to reach the selected stage and send note-off to hear release. The same CC number must be sent; set it before triggering a new note for reliable envelope-stage comparisons.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. For note-start parameters, set MIDI CC 1 before each new note; compare values 0 and 127.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
