                                "value": [ "lfo1_fil1gain=9", "Flexible LFOs / lfoN_filXgain   ·   entry 437", "VALUES: float · -96…96 dB [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Sets LFO N modulation depth for filter X gain.", "Requires lfo1_freq>0 and at least one nonzero destination depth such as lfo1_pitch; waveform/timing settings alone assign no destination. Filter gain needs a shelf/peaking filter type.", "// lfoN_filXgain — Flexible LFOs\n<region>\nsample=*saw lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 lfo1_freq=4 lfo1_wave=1 fil_type=lsh cutoff=600\nresonance=6 lfo1_fil1gain=9\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Flexible LFOs / lfoN_filXgain   ·   entry 437\nVALUES: float · -96…96 dB [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Requires lfo1_freq>0 and at least one nonzero destination depth such as lfo1_pitch; waveform/timing settings alone assign no destination. Filter gain needs a shelf/peaking filter type.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 438,
                                "value": [ "lfo1_fil1gain_oncc1=9", "Flexible LFOs / lfoN_filXgain_onccY   ·   entry 438", "VALUES: float · -96…96 dB [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Sets CC Y control of LFO N modulation depth for filter X gain.", "Requires lfo1_freq>0 and at least one nonzero destination depth such as lfo1_pitch; waveform/timing settings alone assign no destination. Filter gain needs a shelf/peaking filter type. Use MIDI CC 1, matching the numbered suffix; the example supplies its initial value in <control>.", "// lfoN_filXgain_onccY — Flexible LFOs\n<control>\nset_cc1=64\n<region>\nsample=*saw lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 lfo1_freq=4 lfo1_wave=1 lfo1_fil1gain=9 fil_type=lsh\ncutoff=600 resonance=6 lfo1_fil1gain_oncc1=9\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Flexible LFOs / lfoN_filXgain_onccY   ·   entry 438\nVALUES: float · -96…96 dB [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Requires lfo1_freq>0 and at least one nonzero destination depth such as lfo1_pitch; waveform/timing settings alone assign no destination. Filter gain needs a shelf/peaking filter type. Use MIDI CC 1, matching the numbered suffix; the example supplies its initial value in <control>.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
