                                "value": [ "rectify=80", "Effects / rectify   ·   entry 489", "VALUES: float · 0…100 %\nSCOPE: <effect> (effect1…effect4 themselves belong in <region>)", "Sets the proportion of rectified signal mixed into the effect output.", "Requires <effect> type=rectify, bus=fx1, a region effect1 send, and a nonzero fx1tomain return. Parameters after <effect> affect that processor; send opcodes remain under <region>.", "// rectify — Effects\n<effect>\ntype=rectify bus=fx1 rectify_mode=full rectify=80 fx1tomain=100\ndirecttomain=0\n<region>\nsample=*saw lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 effect1=100\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Effects / rectify   ·   entry 489\nVALUES: float · 0…100 %\nSCOPE: <effect> (effect1…effect4 themselves belong in <region>)\nREQUIRES: Requires <effect> type=rectify, bus=fx1, a region effect1 send, and a nonzero fx1tomain return. Parameters after <effect> affect that processor; send opcodes remain under <region>.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 490,
                                "value": [ "gain=-12", "Effects / gain   ·   entry 490", "VALUES: float · -144…48 dB [P]\nSCOPE: <effect> (effect1…effect4 themselves belong in <region>)", "Sets decibel gain in a type=gain effect; upstream source uses the volume specification.", "Requires <effect> type=gain, bus=fx1, a region effect1 send, and a nonzero fx1tomain return. Parameters after <effect> affect that processor; send opcodes remain under <region>.", "// gain — Effects\n<effect>\ntype=gain bus=fx1 gain=-12 fx1tomain=100 directtomain=0\n<region>\nsample=*saw lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 effect1=100\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Effects / gain   ·   entry 490\nVALUES: float · -144…48 dB [P]\nSCOPE: <effect> (effect1…effect4 themselves belong in <region>)\nREQUIRES: Requires <effect> type=gain, bus=fx1, a region effect1 send, and a nonzero fx1tomain return. Parameters after <effect> affect that processor; send opcodes remain under <region>.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 491,
                                "value": [ "width=0", "Effects / width   ·   entry 491", "VALUES: float · -100…100 % [P]\nSCOPE: <effect> (effect1…effect4 themselves belong in <region>)", "Sets stereo width in a type=width effect; 0 is mono and negative values reverse the image.", "Requires <effect> type=width, bus=fx1, a region effect1 send, and a nonzero fx1tomain return. Parameters after <effect> affect that processor; send opcodes remain under <region>. Use a genuinely stereo sample; width does not create an audible width change from identical mono channels. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.", "// width — Effects\n<effect>\ntype=width bus=fx1 width=0 fx1tomain=100 directtomain=0\n<region>\nsample=REPLACE_WITH_STEREO.wav lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-18 ampeg_release=0.25 effect1=100\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Effects / width   ·   entry 491\nVALUES: float · -100…100 % [P]\nSCOPE: <effect> (effect1…effect4 themselves belong in <region>)\nREQUIRES: Requires <effect> type=width, bus=fx1, a region effect1 send, and a nonzero fx1tomain return. Parameters after <effect> affect that processor; send opcodes remain under <region>. Use a genuinely stereo sample; width does not create an audible width change from identical mono channels. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 492,
                                "value": [ "gate_hold=0.15", "Effects / gate_hold   ·   entry 492", "VALUES: float · 0…10 s\nSCOPE: <effect> (effect1…effect4 themselves belong in <region>)", "Sets how long the gate stays open after the signal drops below threshold.", "Requires <effect> type=gate, bus=fx1, a region effect1 send, and a nonzero fx1tomain return. Parameters after <effect> affect that processor; send opcodes remain under <region>.", "// gate_hold — Effects\n<effect>\ntype=gate bus=fx1 gate_threshold=-24 gate_attack=0.01 gate_release=0.3\nfx1tomain=100 gate_hold=0.15 directtomain=0\n<region>\nsample=*saw lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 effect1=100\n", "Play notes at low and high velocities; the input must cross gate_threshold to demonstrate opening/closing.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Effects / gate_hold   ·   entry 492\nVALUES: float · 0…10 s\nSCOPE: <effect> (effect1…effect4 themselves belong in <region>)\nREQUIRES: Requires <effect> type=gate, bus=fx1, a region effect1 send, and a nonzero fx1tomain return. Parameters after <effect> affect that processor; send opcodes remain under <region>.\nTRY: Play notes at low and high velocities; the input must cross gate_threshold to demonstrate opening/closing.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 493,
                                "value": [ "sample_quality=4", "Loading / sample_quality   ·   entry 493", "VALUES: int · 0…10\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Selects the sample interpolation quality; larger values cost more CPU.", "Use a real sample played at a non-native pitch/rate; interpolation differences can be subtle and are not meaningful on a built-in oscillator. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.", "// sample_quality — Loading\n<region>\nsample=REPLACE_WITH_SAMPLE.wav lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60\nvolume=-18 ampeg_release=0.25 transpose=12 sample_quality=4\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Loading / sample_quality   ·   entry 493\nVALUES: int · 0…10\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Use a real sample played at a non-native pitch/rate; interpolation differences can be subtle and are not meaningful on a built-in oscillator. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 494,
                                "value": [ "image=REPLACE_WITH_IMAGE.png", "Loading / image   ·   entry 494", "VALUES: image-file path string [metadata]\nSCOPE: <control>", "In <control>, names an instrument image; Max sfizz~ has no built-in image panel.", "Requires an existing image path; this is metadata and does not create an image display in Max sfizz~. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.", "// image — Loading\n<control>\nimage=REPLACE_WITH_IMAGE.png\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Metadata only; no audible or automatic Max UI response.", "Loading / image   ·   entry 494\nVALUES: image-file path string [metadata]\nSCOPE: <control>\nREQUIRES: Requires an existing image path; this is metadata and does not create an image display in Max sfizz~. Replace every REPLACE_WITH_… filename with a real file path relative to the SFZ.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Metadata only; no audible or automatic Max UI response." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 495,
                                "value": [ "oscillator=on", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator   ·   entry 495", "VALUES: auto | on | off (also 1 | 0)\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Selects automatic, forced-on or forced-off wavetable oscillator playback.", "Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2.", "// oscillator — Wavetable Oscillator\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 oscillator_multi=3 oscillator_detune=20 oscillator=on\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator   ·   entry 495\nVALUES: auto | on | off (also 1 | 0)\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 496,
                                "value": [ "oscillator_detune=20", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator_detune   ·   entry 496", "VALUES: float · -12000…12000 cents [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Sets detuning among the voices of a multi-oscillator region.", "Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2.", "// oscillator_detune — Wavetable Oscillator\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 oscillator=on oscillator_multi=3 oscillator_detune=20\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator_detune   ·   entry 496\nVALUES: float · -12000…12000 cents [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 497,
                                "value": [ "oscillator_detune_oncc1=40", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator_detune_onccN   ·   entry 497", "VALUES: float · -12000…12000 cents [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Uses CC N to change the multi-oscillator detuning amount.", "Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2. Use MIDI CC 1, matching the numbered suffix; the example supplies its initial value in <control>.", "// oscillator_detune_onccN — Wavetable Oscillator\n<control>\nset_cc1=64\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 oscillator=on oscillator_multi=3 oscillator_detune=20\noscillator_detune_oncc1=40\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator_detune_onccN   ·   entry 497\nVALUES: float · -12000…12000 cents [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2. Use MIDI CC 1, matching the numbered suffix; the example supplies its initial value in <control>.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 498,
                                "value": [ "oscillator_mode=2", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator_mode   ·   entry 498", "VALUES: int · 0…2 [!]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Selects normal/ring (0) or modulation (1/2); modes 1 and 2 both run FM in the inspected engine.", "Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2.", "// oscillator_mode — Wavetable Oscillator\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 oscillator=on oscillator_multi=2 oscillator_detune=20\noscillator_mode=2 oscillator_mod_depth=100\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "KNOWN LIMITATION: modes 1 (PM) and 2 (FM) both run FM in the inspected engine.", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator_mode   ·   entry 498\nVALUES: int · 0…2 [!]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: KNOWN LIMITATION: modes 1 (PM) and 2 (FM) both run FM in the inspected engine." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 499,
                                "value": [ "oscillator_mod_depth=100", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator_mod_depth   ·   entry 499", "VALUES: float · 0…10000 % [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Sets the oscillator phase/frequency modulation depth.", "Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2.", "// oscillator_mod_depth — Wavetable Oscillator\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 oscillator=on oscillator_multi=2 oscillator_detune=20\noscillator_mod_depth=100 oscillator_mode=2\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator_mod_depth   ·   entry 499\nVALUES: float · 0…10000 % [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 500,
                                "value": [ "oscillator_mod_depth_oncc1=100", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator_mod_depth_onccN   ·   entry 500", "VALUES: float · 0…10000 % [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Uses CC N to change the oscillator modulation depth.", "Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2. Use MIDI CC 1, matching the numbered suffix; the example supplies its initial value in <control>.", "// oscillator_mod_depth_onccN — Wavetable Oscillator\n<control>\nset_cc1=64\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 oscillator=on oscillator_multi=2 oscillator_detune=20\noscillator_mod_depth_oncc1=100 oscillator_mode=2 oscillator_mod_depth=100\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator_mod_depth_onccN   ·   entry 500\nVALUES: float · 0…10000 % [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2. Use MIDI CC 1, matching the numbered suffix; the example supplies its initial value in <control>.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 501,
                                "value": [ "oscillator_multi=3", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator_multi   ·   entry 501", "VALUES: int · 1…9\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Sets the number of oscillator instances within a voice; upstream ceiling is 9 [B].", "Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2.", "// oscillator_multi — Wavetable Oscillator\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 oscillator=on oscillator_detune=20 oscillator_multi=3\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator_multi   ·   entry 501\nVALUES: int · 1…9\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 502,
                                "value": [ "oscillator_phase=0.25", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator_phase   ·   entry 502", "VALUES: float · 0…1 cycle; negative=random [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Sets initial oscillator phase in cycle fractions in sfizz, rather than degrees.", "Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2. Compare repeated attacks; changing constant phase of a lone steady oscillator is not a useful sustained-tone test.", "// oscillator_phase — Wavetable Oscillator\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 oscillator=on oscillator_multi=3 oscillator_detune=20\noscillator_phase=0.25\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator_phase   ·   entry 502\nVALUES: float · 0…1 cycle; negative=random [P]\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2. Compare repeated attacks; changing constant phase of a lone steady oscillator is not a useful sustained-tone test.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 503,
                                "value": [ "oscillator_quality=3", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator_quality   ·   entry 503", "VALUES: int · 0…3\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)", "Selects oscillator quality from 0 through 3.", "Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2.", "// oscillator_quality — Wavetable Oscillator\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 oscillator=on oscillator_multi=3 oscillator_detune=20\noscillator_quality=3\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build.", "Wavetable Oscillator / oscillator_quality   ·   entry 503\nVALUES: int · 0…3\nSCOPE: <region> (or inherited from <group>/<master>/<global>)\nREQUIRES: Requires an oscillator source (built-in waveform or sample forced into oscillator mode). Detune needs multiple oscillator instances; modulation depth needs oscillator_mode=1 or 2.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Published support table; not runtime-verified for your Max 9 build." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 504,
                                "value": [ "v64=0.2", "Auxiliary engine syntax / vN   ·   entry 504", "VALUES: float · nominal −1…1; N=0…127 [S]\nSCOPE: <curve>", "In <curve>, sets point N; the engine linearly interpolates unspecified points.", "A curve needs curve_index and point values, plus a supported destination_curveccN and a nonzero destination_onccN amount using that same curve index.", "// vN — Auxiliary engine syntax\n<control>\nset_cc1=64\n<curve>\ncurve_index=10 v0=0 v127=1 v64=0.2\n<region>\nsample=*sine lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-36\nampeg_release=0.25 volume_oncc1=30 volume_curvecc1=10\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.", "Upstream-source supplement; availability in your Max 9 binary has not been verified.", "Auxiliary engine syntax / vN   ·   entry 504\nVALUES: float · nominal −1…1; N=0…127 [S]\nSCOPE: <curve>\nREQUIRES: A curve needs curve_index and point values, plus a supported destination_curveccN and a nonzero destination_onccN amount using that same curve index.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release. Sweep MIDI CC 1 while holding a note: midievent 176 1 0 through midievent 176 1 127. set_cc1 is only an initial value and retained CC state can survive reloads.\nBUILD NOTE: Upstream-source supplement; availability in your Max 9 binary has not been verified." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 505,
                                "value": [ "name=embedded_wave.wav", "Auxiliary engine syntax / name   ·   entry 505", "VALUES: sample-name string [S]\nSCOPE: <sample>", "In <sample>, names embedded sample data so a region can refer to it with sample=.", "name and base64data must appear together in <sample>; a region must reference exactly the same sample name. The example embeds a short valid mono WAV.", "// name — Auxiliary engine syntax\n<sample>\nbase64data=UklGRqQAAABXQVZFZm10IBAAAAABAAEAAG4AAADcAAACABAAZGF0YYAAAAAAAK4CVQXvB3YK4wwwD1gRVRMjFbwWHRhDGSoa0Ro2G1gbNhvRGioaQxkdGLwWIxVVE1gRMA/jDHYK7wdVBa4CAABS/av6EfiK9R3z0PCo7qvs3epE6ePnvebW5S/lyuSo5MrkL+XW5b3m4+dE6d3qq+yo7tDwHfOK9RH4q/pS/Q==\nname=embedded_wave.wav\n<region>\nsample=embedded_wave.wav lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 oscillator=on\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Upstream-source supplement; availability in your Max 9 binary has not been verified.", "Auxiliary engine syntax / name   ·   entry 505\nVALUES: sample-name string [S]\nSCOPE: <sample>\nREQUIRES: name and base64data must appear together in <sample>; a region must reference exactly the same sample name. The example embeds a short valid mono WAV.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Upstream-source supplement; availability in your Max 9 binary has not been verified." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 506,
                                "value": [ "base64data=UklGRqQAAABXQVZFZm10IBAAAAABAAEAAG4AAADcAAACABAAZGF0YYAAAAAAAK4CVQXvB3YK4wwwD1gRVRMjFbwWHRhDGSoa0Ro2G1gbNhvRGioaQxkdGLwWIxVVE1gRMA/jDHYK7wdVBa4CAABS/av6EfiK9R3z0PCo7qvs3epE6ePnvebW5S/lyuSo5MrkL+XW5b3m4+dE6d3qq+yo7tDwHfOK9RH4q/pS/Q==", "Auxiliary engine syntax / base64data   ·   entry 506", "VALUES: base64-encoded audio-file data [S]\nSCOPE: <sample>", "In <sample>, embeds a base64 audio file; bare data= is not decoded by this engine.", "name and base64data must appear together in <sample>; a region must reference exactly the same sample name. The example embeds a short valid mono WAV.", "// base64data — Auxiliary engine syntax\n<sample>\nname=embedded_wave.wav\nbase64data=UklGRqQAAABXQVZFZm10IBAAAAABAAEAAG4AAADcAAACABAAZGF0YYAAAAAAAK4CVQXvB3YK4wwwD1gRVRMjFbwWHRhDGSoa0Ro2G1gbNhvRGioaQxkdGLwWIxVVE1gRMA/jDHYK7wdVBa4CAABS/av6EfiK9R3z0PCo7qvs3epE6ePnvebW5S/lyuSo5MrkL+XW5b3m4+dE6d3qq+yo7tDwHfOK9RH4q/pS/Q==\n<region>\nsample=embedded_wave.wav lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 oscillator=on\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Upstream-source supplement; availability in your Max 9 binary has not been verified.", "Auxiliary engine syntax / base64data   ·   entry 506\nVALUES: base64-encoded audio-file data [S]\nSCOPE: <sample>\nREQUIRES: name and base64data must appear together in <sample>; a region must reference exactly the same sample name. The example embeds a short valid mono WAV.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Upstream-source supplement; availability in your Max 9 binary has not been verified." ]
                            },
                            {
                                "key": 507,
                                "value": [ "sfizz:filter_gain=9", "Auxiliary engine syntax / sfizz:filter_gain   ·   entry 507", "VALUES: float · −96…96 dB [P] [S]\nSCOPE: <effect> (effect1…effect4 themselves belong in <region>)", "In <effect> type=filter, sets shelf/peak gain; this is the implemented spelling behind filter_gain.", "Requires <effect> type=filter, bus=fx1, a region effect1 send, and a nonzero fx1tomain return. Parameters after <effect> affect that processor; send opcodes remain under <region>.", "// sfizz:filter_gain — Auxiliary engine syntax\n<effect>\ntype=filter bus=fx1 filter_type=lsh filter_cutoff=800 filter_resonance=9\nfx1tomain=100 sfizz:filter_gain=9 directtomain=0\n<region>\nsample=*saw lokey=48 hikey=72 pitch_keycenter=60 volume=-18\nampeg_release=0.25 effect1=100\n", "Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.", "Upstream-source supplement; availability in your Max 9 binary has not been verified.", "Auxiliary engine syntax / sfizz:filter_gain   ·   entry 507\nVALUES: float · −96…96 dB [P] [S]\nSCOPE: <effect> (effect1…effect4 themselves belong in <region>)\nREQUIRES: Requires <effect> type=filter, bus=fx1, a region effect1 send, and a nonzero fx1tomain return. Parameters after <effect> affect that processor; send opcodes remain under <region>.\nTRY: Load this SFZ into sfizz~; enable audio; play MIDI note 60 at velocity 100, hold for 2 seconds, then release.\nBUILD NOTE: Upstream-source supplement; availability in your Max 9 binary has not been verified." ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
