                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "menu-1",
                    "items": [ "Choose an opcode…", ",", "Defines a preprocessor substitution; this directive does not use an equals sign.  [#define]", ",", "In <control>; sets the base directory for sample-file references.  [default_path]", ",", "In <control>; shifts mapped note numbers by this many semitones.  [note_offset]", ",", "In <control>; shifts mapped note numbers by this many octaves.  [octave_offset]", ",", "In <control>; assigns metadata text to a controller; Max has no automatic label display.  [label_ccN]", ",", "In <control>; assigns metadata text to a MIDI key; this does not alter its pitch.  [label_keyN]", ",", "In <control>; supplies a controller initial value; retained MIDI state can affect reload behavior.  [set_ccN]", ",", "Inserts another SFZ text file at this position; this directive does not use an equals sign.  [#include]", ",", "In <control>; supplies a normalized high-resolution controller initial value.  [set_hdccN]", ",", "In <control>; supplies a normalized high-resolution controller initial value.  [set_realccN]", ",", "In <control>; selects how the engine chooses a voice to steal at the voice limit.  [hint_stealing]", ",", "In <control>; requests whole samples in RAM instead of normal disk streaming.  [hint_ram_based]", ",", "In <control>; allows a newly pressed sustain pedal to cancel a voice release.  [hint_sustain_cancels_release]" ],
                    "maxclass": "umenu",
