            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 13.0,
                    "id": "obj-152",
                    "linecount": 3,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 24.0, 2105.0, 1360.0, 50.0 ],
                    "text": "DATA SCHEMA — embedded coll, one numeric key per entry; each field is one symbol. 1 expression; 2 title; 3 range/scope; 4 function; 5 dependencies; 6 multiline SFZ; 7 test action; 8 compatibility note; 9 combined documentation. Edit a coll row to customize a recipe, then save this patch. Initialization selects lfoN_freq and emits its record. Optional inlet recall does not change the menu label. Patching mode exposes the inlet/outlets and data store; presentation mode is the browser. No external scripts, samples or coll files are needed to open the browser."
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 13.0,
                    "id": "obj-153",
                    "linecount": 3,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 24.0, 2210.0, 1360.0, 50.0 ],
                    "text": "SCOPE / VALIDATION — 503 published support-table rows plus the four auxiliary fields already in the earlier index. Parameter families are represented once with N/X/Y placeholders; examples resolve them to concrete indices. This is not a claim that every current upstream feature is supported by every Max 9 binary. Source: sfz.tools/sfizz/development/status/opcodes/, Cycling ’74 sfizz~ reference, upstream sfizz f5c6e29f23b8057867c08e88f5f6ac6738baa30b, and SFZ Format CC0 documentation. Static data/connection/layout checks only; Max runtime was unavailable."
                }
            }
